2026-10-18T12:07:06.6509063Z -- Building presets (item 17)
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6509410Z   ok   a masonry house has more thermal mass than a timber one
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6509766Z   ok   an older house loses more heat
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6510061Z   ok   loss scales with heated area
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6510379Z   ok   floor heating adds an actively charged store
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6510736Z   ok   radiators respond faster than floor heating
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6511172Z   ok   timber-on-slab over a crawl space is the crawl-space house, exactly
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6511648Z   ok   the subtraction only fires under a crawl-space foundation
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6512129Z   ok   masonry over a crawl space keeps its walls -- nothing was removed twice
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6512653Z   ok   a concrete slab over a crawl space loses the slab but keeps the concrete
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6513229Z   ok   a heated basement adds both mass and loss
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6513626Z   ok   the heavy mass lives in the heated slab, and only there
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6514023Z   ok   the radiator power fraction follows the emitters
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6514427Z   ok   a radiator loop is a small store, not the building's slab
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6514894Z   ok   radiators can deliver the design heat load at a sane flow temperature
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6515386Z   ok   with radiators the heavy floor coasts as part of the room store
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6515824Z   ok   nonsense options are clamped rather than propagated
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6516278Z   ok   a valid non-radiator emitter is kept, only an unknown one is clamped
2026-10-18T12:07:06.6516720Z   ok   derived values are accepted by the thermal model
